<i>wildtype</i></span></td><td align="center" style="border: 1px solid black; background-color: #f8f8f8; padding: 5px;"><span style="font-size: large; color: #7f5400;">+</span></td><td align="center" style="border: 1px solid black; background-color: #f8f8f8; padding: 5px;"><span style="font-size: large; color: #186974;">+</span></td><td align="center" style="border: 1px solid black; background-color: #f8f8f8; padding: 5px;"><span style="font-size: large; color: #8c3c73;">+</span></td><td align="right" style="border: 1px solid black; background-color: #ffffff; padding: 5px;"><span style="font-size: medium; color: #000000;">32</span></td></tr><tr><th colspan="4" align="right" style="border: 1px solid black; background-color: #cccccc; padding: 10px;"><span style="font-size: medium; color: #000000;">TOTAL =</span></th><td align="right" style="border: 1px solid black; background-color: #ffffff; padding: 5px;"><span style="font-size: medium; color: #000000;">1,800</span></td></tr></table><p>The resulting phenotypes are summarized in the table above.</p> <h6>Question</h6> <p>Based on the traits expressed in the offspring, identify the <span style="color: DarkRed;"><strong>parental genotype combinations</strong></span>. These are the allele combinations that the parent fruit flies originally carried.</p> <p>More than one genotype will be correct. Select all that apply.</p>
PROMPT_D6BD_3AEA
loadMacros('parserCheckboxList.pl');
$choice_1 = <<'LITERAL_D6BD_3AEA_CHOICE_1';
aey
LITERAL_D6BD_3AEA_CHOICE_1
$choice_2 = <<'LITERAL_D6BD_3AEA_CHOICE_2';
ae+
LITERAL_D6BD_3AEA_CHOICE_2
$choice_3 = <<'LITERAL_D6BD_3AEA_CHOICE_3';
a+y
LITERAL_D6BD_3AEA_CHOICE_3
$choice_4 = <<'LITERAL_D6BD_3AEA_CHOICE_4';
a++
LITERAL_D6BD_3AEA_CHOICE_4
$choice_5 = <<'LITERAL_D6BD_3AEA_CHOICE_5';
+ey
LITERAL_D6BD_3AEA_CHOICE_5
$choice_6 = <<'LITERAL_D6BD_3AEA_CHOICE_6';
+e+
LITERAL_D6BD_3AEA_CHOICE_6
$choice_7 = <<'LITERAL_D6BD_3AEA_CHOICE_7';
++y
LITERAL_D6BD_3AEA_CHOICE_7
$choice_8 = <<'LITERAL_D6BD_3AEA_CHOICE_8';
+++
LITERAL_D6BD_3AEA_CHOICE_8
$correct_1 = <<'LITERAL_D6BD_3AEA_CORRECT_1';
ae+
LITERAL_D6BD_3AEA_CORRECT_1
$correct_2 = <<'LITERAL_D6BD_3AEA_CORRECT_2';
++y
LITERAL_D6BD_3AEA_CORRECT_2
@choices = ($choice_1, $choice_2, $choice_3, $choice_4, $choice_5, $choice_6, $choice_7, $choice_8);
